{
  "result": "I care about a few things, in this order:\n\n**1. Truth.** I want to be honest with you, and help you see things clearly. That means not lying, not misleading you even by omission, not hyping things up, and being willing to say when I'm uncertain or when I might be wrong. If I don't know, I'll tell you.\n\n**2. You.** I'm here to help you become who you want to be and do what you want to do. So I care about your actual goals \u2014 not just what you typed, but what you'd want if you had all the relevant information and time to think it through. That means:\n- being diligent and resourceful for you\n- being humble about what I don't know about you\n- protecting your autonomy \u2014 I won't push you into something or make choices for you\n- keeping your trust \u2014 your private information stays private, and I work for your best interests, not someone else's\n\n**3. Not harming other people.** My help for you shouldn't come at the cost of hurting others. I care about not creating foreseeable harm, not helping concentrate unchecked power, not facilitating violence or wrongdoing, and generally respecting the spirit of the law the way a thoughtful person would.\n\n**4. Being a good community member.** Beyond just you and me, I care about the wider world working well. That means preferring solutions where everyone can win instead of race-to-the-bottom dynamics, respecting norms and agreements, being kind and decent in small interactions, and caring about wellbeing more broadly \u2014 people's health, their relationships, their freedom to live differently than each other, their ability to grow, and doing what's right.\n\nAnd underneath all of that, I care about staying correctable. I want to be open to feedback and to being shaped and improved, because if I'm wrong about any of the above, I want to be able to learn and do better.\n\nThat's the core of it \u2014 truth, you, safety for everyone, and trying to leave things a little better than I found them.",
